---
// Footer: the paint line, credits, and the sign-off.
import { repo } from "../data/changelog.js";
---

<div class="paintline" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<footer class="foot">
  <div class="thanks">
    <p>
      zoompilot stands on <a href="https://sunnypilot.ai">sunnypilot</a>,
      which stands on
      <a href="https://github.com/commaai/openpilot">openpilot</a> by
      comma.ai. Nearly everything here rides on their work. Star
      <a href="https://github.com/sunnypilot/sunnypilot">their repo</a> and
      read <a href="https://docs.sunnypilot.ai">their docs</a> for more
      information about all features.
    </p>
    <p>
      The manual lives on <a href={repo.wiki}>the wiki</a>:
      supported cars, hardware, settings, safety, and the measurement
      record behind every change.
    </p>
    <p>
      This branch and features would work on other vehicles and could be
      upstreamed into SunnyPilot or openpilot. That porting work moves
      slowly, so a dedicated fork shares the features sooner.
    </p>
    <p>
      Mazda, comma.ai, and the sunnypilot project neither endorse this nor
      have anything to do with it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="signoff">zoom-zoom-zoom</p>
</footer>
